        "id": 3788053
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-08-19T16:13:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "GPU generation in number is a good concept to group a bunch of GPUs with the same architectures and ease the way to work around issues. For example, QC devices have maxStorageBufferBindingSize issue and it will be fixed in the next release of new device. With generation, it will be easy to work around it with generation \u003c\u003d 7 (Adreno 7xx). Intel also has many workarounds, which could be rewritten in this way for simplicity. \nSo I introduced GPU generation concept here, and implement it for both QC and Intel.",
      "revId": "5b1feff0b0b7776f3791b85623a8fe29b253643b",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
